Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Build a 5-bit ring counter with synchronous active low reset signal. The ring counter circulates a single high bit through the 5-bit counter.
// (1) reset_n: Resets the ring counter to 5'b00001 when low.
// (2) q: The current state of the ring counter.

module ring_counter(
    input clk,
    input reset_n,
    output reg [4:0] q);

code:
module ring_counter(
    input clk,
    input reset_n,
    output reg [4:0] q
);

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!reset_n) begin
            // Synchronous reset: Reset the ring counter to 5'b00001
            q <= 5'b00001;
        end else begin
            // Ring operation: Circulate the high bit
            q <= {q[3:0], q[4]};
        end
    end

endmodule

