Design a one-bit full adder circuit that computes the sum of three input bits: `a`, `b`, and `cin` (carry-in). The module outputs a single-bit sum and a carry-out (`cout`). The sum is calculated using the XOR operation, while the carry-out is generated based on the logical AND and XOR operations among the inputs, effectively determining if a carry should be propagated to the next higher bit.
